# options_trader_v3/.gitignore
# 2026-08-13 — repaired three defects found while inventorying box artifacts:
#   (1) `*.ziptrades.db-shm` was a MISSING NEWLINE, so `*.zip` was never actually
#       ignored and `trades.db-shm` was only covered by the earlier `*.db-shm`.
#   (2) `orb_range.json echo analysis/orb_range.json` captured a stray `echo`
#       from a bad `>>` append; it matched a filename nobody will ever create.
#   (3) `data/feed_store.db` was NOT ignored while `trades.db` was — a `git add -A`
#       on a box would have committed a multi-MB binary SQLite DB.
# Secrets — never commit these
credentials.py
cred.txt
# One-shot deploy bootstrap holding real secrets — never commit. Any bootstrap*.sh
# is ignored EXCEPT the placeholder template, which is the committed reference.
bootstrap*.sh
!bootstrap.example.sh
*.pem
*.key
*.env

# Database and logs — generated at runtime
trades.db
data/feed_store.db
bot.log
*.log
*.log.*
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Candle logger output — generated at runtime (in-project data dir)
data/OHLC/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
venv/
env/
.venv/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Archives
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
trades.db-shm
trades.db-wal
orb_range.json
orb_state.json
ohlc/
*.csv

# Shadow observer output — generated at runtime (in-project data dir)
data/shadow/
data/signal_journal/
# LIQ.4 output - written every closed bar once the ledger is live.
# NOT scaffolding to clean up: it is the running record. It must never be
# committed, and `git add -A` in a deploy line would sweep it in.
data/liquidity_ledger/
*.patch
data/chain_snapshots/
MANIFEST.txt

# 2026-08-18 (fork): SMC core book — per-box state, never committed
data/smc_state.json
